# Which program opens what, as this desktop ships.
#
# The menu hands a line that matched no application to the web, and the guide
# and the settings have links in them. Every one of those asks xdg-open rather
# than naming a browser, so the name is written here once and nothing else on
# the machine holds a second copy of it.
#
# It has to be said. There are three browsers on this device and the desktop
# picks between them by what was installed last, which is not a decision
# anybody made. librewolf is the one the palette was written for; chromium is
# kept for the site that will not work in it and is not the one a link should
# land in.
#
# Here rather than under her own config, because the settings panel writes that
# one and this is the answer it starts from. XDG reads hers first and falls
# back to this, so choosing a browser on the Web tab is a file of her own laid
# over this one, and a machine put back together from the manifest still opens
# a link in something.
# Music is here for the same reason and a sharper one. A browser says it opens
# audio, because a browser can play a sound in a page, so a song opened from
# the files panel landed in one: a whole window, a black rectangle with a
# scrubber in it, and nothing on this device that knows what album it is from.
#
# An `.opus` file is the case that made it obvious. It is not `audio/ogg` to
# the mime database, it is `audio/x-opus+ogg`, and nothing on this machine had
# ever said that type out loud -- not the music panel's own desktop file, not
# the settings, not here -- so it fell through everything to whatever claimed
# it last. The rule is that a kind of thing is a family of types and every one
# of them has to be named, because the one that is left out is the one that
# opens somewhere surprising.
[Default Applications]
text/html=librewolf.desktop
x-scheme-handler/http=librewolf.desktop
x-scheme-handler/https=librewolf.desktop
audio/mpeg=console-music.desktop
audio/flac=console-music.desktop
audio/ogg=console-music.desktop
audio/x-opus+ogg=console-music.desktop
audio/x-vorbis+ogg=console-music.desktop
audio/x-flac+ogg=console-music.desktop
audio/mp4=console-music.desktop
audio/aac=console-music.desktop
audio/vnd.wave=console-music.desktop
